4
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:20,060
First Lady Melania Trump has led all of the preparation for the state visit,

5
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:26,640
which will honor the longstanding and special relationship between the United States and the United Kingdom.

6
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:34,360
As I told many of you on Friday afternoon, I thought that would be my last time taking your questions until after my maternity leave.

7
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:40,940
But given the attempted assassination of the president and, quote, top Trump administration officials,

8
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:47,940
as the depraved shooter noted in his manifesto at the White House Correspondents Association dinner on Saturday evening,

9
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:58,200
I felt it was prudent to be here today to answer your questions and inform the American people about how the administration is responding to yet another attempt on President Trump's life.

10
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:06,600
Saturday was supposed to be a joyful evening, celebrating free speech in the First Amendment with all of you, members of the press.

11
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:18,600
Instead, the night was hijacked by a crazed anti-Trump individual who traveled across the country to assassinate the president and as many administration officials as possible.

12
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:23,860
This is the third major assassination attempt against President Trump in two years.

13
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:30,180
No other president in history has faced such repeated, serious attempts on his life.

14
00:01:30,580 --> 00:01:44,260
First and foremost, the President, the First Lady, and everyone in this White House are extraordinarily grateful to the brave law enforcement professionals who's spraying into action to apprehend the would-be assassin and keep all of us safe.

15
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:50,800
The President would especially like to express his gratitude to the men and women of the United States Secret Service,

16
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:55,420
who acted with the utmost professionalism, courage, and sense of duty.

17
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:59,940
This includes the heroic agent who took a bullet to the chest.

18
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:02,720
Thankfully, he was saved by his bulletproof vest.

19
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:06,160
Minutes after returning here to the White House to the Oval Office,

20
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:10,920
despite fighting Secret Service to try to stay and keep the dinner going on Saturday,

21
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:13,640
ahead of addressing you here in the briefing room,

22
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:18,760
President Trump was intent on speaking to this brave agent to ensure he was okay,

23
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:21,580
and the agent assured the president that he was.

24
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:30,340
As you know, I was seated next to President Trump and the First Lady when the shots were fired before Secret Service swiftly moved us to safety backstage.

25
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:40,700
The President's calm in the face of chaos, while yet another individual was trying to take his life, was really remarkable to witness, and it's something I will never forget.

26
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:54,540
President Trump is fearless because he loves this country and he is willing to put his own life on the line to deliver on the promises that he made to the American public who elected him here into the highest office in the land.

27
00:02:54,820 --> 00:03:06,280
And while we are blessed to have a fearless president, we should not live in a country where such constant fear of political violence permeates our society every single day.

28
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:10,640
We can and we should have fierce disagreement in this country.

29
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:15,380
As you all know, we disagree often, myself and this role, and all of you in the news media.

30
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:18,180
But those disagreements must remain peaceful.

31
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:24,560
Debating, peaceful protesting, and voting are how we need to settle disagreements, not bullets.

32
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:30,100
Nobody in recent years has faced more bullets and more violence than President Trump.

33
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:42,520
This political violence stems from a systemic demonization of him and his supporters, by commentators, yes, by elected members of the Democrat Party and even some in the media.

34
00:03:42,540 --> 00:03:54,920
This hateful and constant and violent rhetoric directed at President Trump day after day after day for 11 years has helped legitimize this violence and bring us to this dark moment.

35
00:03:55,240 --> 00:04:07,640
Those who constantly falsely label and slander the president as a fascist, as a threat to democracy, and compare him to Hitler to score political points are fueling this kind of violence.

36
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:19,400
The left-wing cult of hatred against the president, and all of those who support him and work for him has gotten multiple people hurt and killed, and it almost did so again this weekend.

37
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:23,720
When you read the manifesto of this shooter, ask yourselves,

38
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:28,960
how different is the rhetoric from this almost assassin than what you read on social media

39
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:32,740
